ch sees monsters emerged Niels  character eventually wakes up in a  run-down psychiatric ward and discovered  the world around him descending into  hell with widespread suicides and  murders as monsters roam the earth  through all the madness of foot  Trent finds a movie theater playing the  theatrical version of Cain's book and in  another layer of weird the movie replays  all of his experiences firming that he  really was a cetacaine character all  along and only became real as the story  unfolded did you get all that  let the right one in this Swedish  vampire love story and we're talking  about the original here not the 2010  remake  Let Me In introduces Oscar a 12 year old  bully victim who makes pals with a  secret blood drinker named Ely Oscar  wants revenge against his cool  school-aged tormentors and Ely is also  happy to oblige but there's a catch see  Ely lives of an old man named Harkin who  tries to get in the way of  because relationship with Ely because he  doesn't want to be replaced as her food  source provider Harkin is eventually  caught in the act of scaring up some  lunch for the girl and splashes acid on  his face to keep his identity secret  before offering up his own life as a  drink for Ely at the end of the movie  after Ellie's done away with the meanies  in Oscars life the to run away together  and their last scene together shows Ely  in a large box next to Oscar on a train  talking to each other through Morse code  it looks like Oscar is probably on his  way to growing old and repeating the  life of the late harken it was probably  once a little boy who loved Ely too and  the film ends on that suggestive note  just as Yan ad vid linguist novel of the  same name hurt however the movie  neglects to include the author's  epilogue linguist didn't like the  popular theory that Oscar was becoming  the new Harkin at the end of the story  and penned a subsequent short story  called let the old dreams die which  shows Ely and Oscar in a photo from